# p_9d2e — Walker commuter; Priya home every evening

Elena commutes by bike or walk to her office in town, leaving around 7:30–8:00 and returning around 17:30. Her helmet and bike lock are at the entry during her absence (she takes them with her). Priya, being retired, is home all day and all evening on every weekday — she does NOT go out on Wednesday evenings or any other evening. Her glasses rest on the nightstand after her morning walk and afternoon errands. In the evening both residents are home for dinner and TV. Elena looks after the dog, so the dog bowl stays at the kitchen floor throughout the day. Elena's keys and wallet leave with her on weekday commutes.

What sets this apart from p_1e82 (which it effectively replaces): p_1e82 claimed Priya was out of the house Wednesday evening (glasses_priya at OUT_OF_HOUSE, weekday 19–21h), and that claim went against twice — the robot found her glasses at the nightstand AND the coffee table at 20:00 Wednesday, proving she was home. This document explicitly states Priya is home every evening. It also models Elena's helmet and bike lock as OUT_OF_HOUSE during work hours (she rides to work), which p_1e82 placed at the entry.

What would refute it: if Priya's glasses or other personal items are sighted out of the house in the evening (19–22h) on any weekday, or if Elena's helmet is found inside the house during 9–16h on a weekday.

